  "summary_en": "Draft Drone Rules, 2021 published by India's Ministry of Civil Aviation for comment, superseding the UAS Rules 2021. They set weight-based drone classes, airworthiness certification, registration, remote pilot licensing, red/yellow/green airspace zones, traffic management, third-party insurance, penalties and a promotion council.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Drones classified into nano, micro, small, medium, large by weight",
   "Type certificate of airworthiness via Quality Council of India; unique ID registration on Digital Sky platform",
   "Remote pilot licence required except nano and non-commercial micro drones",
   "Red/yellow/green airspace zoning with prior permission required in red and yellow zones",
   "Third-party insurance per Motor Vehicles Act; penalties up to one lakh rupees; Drone Promotion Council"
  ],
